  "articleBody": "While minor paint touch-ups are common weekend tasks, comprehensive interior painting often reveals technical challenges that call for an experienced contractor.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\n- Pre-1978 home renovations: For paid work disturbing painted surfaces in older homes, EPA Renovation, Repair and Painting rules require lead-safe certified firms, proper containment, and specialized cleanup procedures.\n- Widespread peeling or drywall water stains: Flaking layers and water stains require drywall repairs and stain-blocking primers before painting.\n- Tall ceilings and complex stairwells: Vaulted foyers demand proper staging and safety equipment to reach trim smoothly without injury.\n- Large multi-room transformations: Keeping a uniform sheen and seamless cut-in lines across joined open spaces requires steady technique and proper equipment.\n- Full trim and casing overhauls: Painting detailed woodwork and moldings demands clean brushwork and smooth enamel applications.\n\nWhat to Do Next\nIf your home demands extensive drywall patching or full interior finish work, get in touch with owner Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC by calling 303-505-0866 to review your interior painting plans.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}